{"skill":{"slug":"obsidian-direct","displayName":"Obsidian - read, search, write and edit direct to obsidian vault."},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770331850180,"changelog":"Initial release — Adds support for managing Obsidian vaults as a knowledge base.\n\n- Fuzzy/phonetic search across all notes using fast ripgrep filtering.\n- Automatic folder detection for new notes and note suggestion based on content.\n- Create, read, and edit notes with frontmatter (timestamps, tags, aliases).\n- Manage tags, incoming/outgoing wikilinks, and sections within notes.\n- Comprehensive CLI scripts for querying, saving, editing, and organizing notes and folders.\n- Designed workflows for knowledge base queries, note creation, and prompt-driven editing.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3548,"sha256":"2ad18a71252d114c58094a4c8ded4441c889184749264ea2888cfecb2c1e1d04","contentType":null},{"path":"_meta.json","size":127,"sha256":"097709ff9fc7c56a4645ec8544be578ca7c23a086fe2c1ae2b6a5add670c43d7","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/obsidian_cli.py","size":13649,"sha256":"f1d548880fcf392bed34597dbb055ce5f5bea62e7ba0b5ba46b437063b39be66","contentType":"text/x-python"},{"path":"scripts/obsidian_search.py","size":8329,"sha256":"11fe1482630a351ef90c4bd485a5a338838fa2abd4b843e8f96c96319099e6f0","contentType":"text/x-python"},{"path":".clawhub/origin.json","size":140,"sha256":"796fe42e30e5b25b7a7b37ece705f00f08ba304a12a3fa25f1657df91902cd98","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1954,"sha256":"27b0ce8a1eac018dacd6a8cac5e813c075713eb0b10336d19f889ce76004ec32","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789035791505,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"fb39d645fc60d322d1e6f7f66310b31d7ff07f534bde47a7ec5076a0b906ed97","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/fb39d645fc60d322d1e6f7f66310b31d7ff07f534bde47a7ec5076a0b906ed97","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: obsidian-direct\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe OpenClaw AgentSkills skill bundle for Obsidian is classified as benign. The `SKILL.md` provides clear, task-oriented instructions for the agent to manage Obsidian notes, without any evidence of prompt injection attempts to deviate from its purpose or perform malicious actions. The Python scripts (`obsidian_cli.py`, `obsidian_search.py`) legitimately interact with the file system to read and write markdown files within the specified vault. Crucially, external command execution via `subprocess.run` (for `ripgrep` and `grep`) properly sanitizes user input using `re.escape()`, mitigating command injection risks. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, persistence mechanisms, or other malicious behaviors.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779077869411},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":11,"checkedAt":1789035791505},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This Obsidian skill does match its stated purpose, but its file handling can escape the intended vault boundary and modify persistent local files.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Filesystem access to an Obsidian vault is proportionate for the purpose, but the implementation does not enforce the vault boundary before listing, creating, reading, or editing Markdown files.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The package contains a SKILL.md, metadata, and two local Python scripts, with no install hook, remote payload retrieval, dependency installer, or service setup observed.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill documents create and edit workflows, including replace-style edits, but it does not clearly require confirmation for destructive note overwrites or warn agents to constrain folders to vault-relative paths.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No privilege escalation or background persistence was found, but create/edit operations persistently write files and the replace/clear actions can overwrite note contents without an explicit safety gate.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is to search, read, create, and edit Obsidian Markdown notes, and the bundled scripts implement those capabilities; however, user-controlled folder paths and symlinked notes can extend reads or writes outside the intended vault.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable giving the skill read/write access to your Obsidian vault. Before use, restrict it to a specific vault path, avoid passing untrusted folder or note names, keep backups, and require confirmation before replace, clear, or broad edit operations.","findings":"[TP4] expected: The scanner concern about unseen scripts is downgraded because the referenced scripts are present and were inspected; fixed local vault and script paths are disclosed, though not ideal for portability or scoping.\n[SDI-1] unexpected: The path traversal concern is supported by artifact code: folder input is joined with the vault without canonical confinement before listing or creating notes.\n[LP3] expected: Shell and filesystem use are expected for a local Obsidian integration, but the lack of explicit vault-boundary enforcement and read/write separation remains a review concern.\n[SQP-2] expected: Creating and editing notes is expected, but replace and clear operations overwrite persistent content without prominent warning or confirmation guidance.\n[AE4] expected: Unicode normalization and Russian transliteration appear purpose-aligned with the documented fuzzy/phonetic RU-to-EN search behavior; no obfuscation or evasion behavior was found.\n[AST4] expected: The rg and grep subprocess calls are expected search helpers and use argument lists with escaped patterns rather than shell execution, so command-injection risk is downgraded.\n[SQP-3] expected: Russian examples are present, but they appear to be examples for note-editing prompts rather than an instruction to force a language.\n[T05] unexpected: The static vault-boundary bypass finding is supported: absolute or traversal folder values and symlinked Markdown notes can cause access outside the configured vault under the agent process permissions.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789035791505}}}}}